# Said instead of an Uninstall button on an app that the computer cannot work without.
common-removal-needed = No se puede desinstalar: el equipo lo necesita

# Said instead of an Uninstall button on an app whose removal would take a part of Trindle with it.
common-removal-trindle-needs = No se puede desinstalar: una parte de Trindle lo necesita

# Name of the updates button, and its tip, while the ring's own update button is putting updates in.
common-updating-short-ring = Actualizando

# Name of an update button while Apps is putting updates in.
common-updating-short-apps = Actualizando en Aplicaciones

# Name of an update button while the daily security fixes for the apps' boxes are going in.
common-updating-short-boxes = Instalando correcciones de seguridad

# Name of an update button while Debian's own installer is at work.
common-updating-short-system = Debian se está actualizando

# Name of an update button while something not named is installing updates.
common-updating-short-unknown = Actualizando en otro lugar

# Headline of an updates page while the ring is installing updates.
common-updating-sentence-ring = Se están instalando actualizaciones desde el anillo.

# Headline of an updates page while Apps is installing updates.
common-updating-sentence-apps = Se están instalando actualizaciones desde Aplicaciones.

# Headline of an updates page while the daily security fixes are going into the apps' boxes.
common-updating-sentence-boxes = Se están instalando correcciones de seguridad en las cajas de las aplicaciones.

# Headline of an updates page while Debian's installer is at work (the daily security updates, apt in a terminal, or another person).
common-updating-sentence-system = El instalador de Debian está trabajando, como cada día con las actualizaciones de seguridad.

# Headline of an updates page while something not named is installing updates.
common-updating-sentence-unknown = Se están instalando actualizaciones en otro lugar.

# Beside an app in a list of updates, when what waits is a newer build of the version already installed. { $version } is the version.
common-updating-newer-build-of = una compilación más reciente de la versión { $version }

# Beside an app in a list of updates: the installed version, then the version that waits.
common-updating-version-to = versión { $from } a { $to }

# Beside an app in a list of updates, when only the installed version is known. { $version } is that version.
common-updating-now-version = ahora versión { $version }

# Beside an app in a list of updates, when only the new version is known. { $version } is that version.
common-updating-to-version = a la versión { $version }

# Beside a thing whose own version is shown, when what waits is a newer build of the same version.
common-updating-newer-waiting = hay una compilación más reciente en espera

# Beside a thing whose own version is shown: the version that waits.
common-updating-version-waiting = la versión { $version } está en espera

# Beside a thing whose own version is shown, when the new version is not known.
common-updating-update-waiting = hay una actualización en espera

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Said in the password box when Debian's and Trindle's updates are put in together.
common-updating-reason-all = Las actualizaciones de Debian y de Trindle cambian todo el equipo, para todos los que lo usan, así que necesitan la contraseña de administrador. Las aplicaciones que instalaste tú se actualizan sin ella.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Said in the password box when only Debian's updates are put in.
common-updating-reason-debian = Las actualizaciones de Debian cambian todo el equipo, para todos los que lo usan, así que necesitan la contraseña de administrador.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Said in the password box when only Trindle's own update is put in.
common-updating-reason-trindle = La actualización de Trindle cambia todo el equipo, para todos los que lo usan, así que necesita la contraseña de administrador.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Said in the password box when new firmware is put in.
common-updating-reason-firmware = El firmware nuevo cambia el propio equipo, así que necesita la contraseña de administrador.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Said in the password box when the lists of the whole computer's updates are fetched away from the computer's own screen.
common-updating-reason-refresh = Buscar las actualizaciones de todo el equipo necesita la contraseña de administrador cuando no se pide desde la pantalla del propio equipo.

# The end of a sentence saying why nothing was installed. { $why } is the reason, such as "no administrator's password was given".
common-updating-because = porque { $why }.

# Red words beside an update that did not finish and gave no reason.
common-updating-no-reason = No terminó, y no dio ningún motivo.

# Red words beside an update that did not finish. { $why } is the reason the system gave.
common-updating-failed = No terminó. { $why }

# Red words beside an update that was never started. { $why } is the end of a sentence such as "because no administrator's password was given."
common-updating-not-installed = No se instaló, { $why }

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# End of a sentence saying why a step was refused: the password box was closed. It follows "because".
common-refused-why-cancelled = no se dio ninguna contraseña de administrador

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# End of a sentence saying why a step was refused: the password was asked for and not accepted. It follows "because".
common-refused-why-wrong = no se aceptó la contraseña de administrador

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# End of a sentence saying why a step was refused: this login may never do it. It follows "because".
common-refused-why-not-allowed = esta sesión no tiene permiso para hacerlo, sea cual sea la contraseña

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# End of a sentence saying why a step was refused: nothing was there to ask for the password. It follows "because".
common-refused-why-unasked = no había nada que pidiera la contraseña de administrador

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# End of a sentence saying why a step was refused: it is not known which of the two reasons it was. It follows "because".
common-refused-why-unclear = no se aceptó la contraseña de administrador, o esta sesión no tiene permiso para hacerlo

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Sentence of its own saying a step was refused: the password box was closed.
common-refused-sentence-cancelled = No se dio ninguna contraseña de administrador

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Sentence of its own saying a step was refused: the password was not accepted.
common-refused-sentence-wrong = No se aceptó la contraseña de administrador

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Sentence of its own saying a step was refused: this login may never do it.
common-refused-sentence-not-allowed = Esta sesión no tiene permiso para hacerlo, sea cual sea la contraseña

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Sentence of its own saying a step was refused: nothing was there to ask for the password.
common-refused-sentence-unasked = No había nada que pidiera la contraseña de administrador

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Sentence of its own saying a step was refused: it is not known which of the two reasons it was.
common-refused-sentence-unclear = No se aceptó la contraseña de administrador, o esta sesión no tiene permiso para hacerlo

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Red words when a step was refused because the password box was closed.
common-refused-not-done-cancelled = No se hizo: no se dio ninguna contraseña de administrador.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Red words when a step was refused because the password was not accepted.
common-refused-not-done-wrong = No se hizo: no se aceptó la contraseña de administrador.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Red words when a step was refused because this login may never do it; the last sentence says what may help.
common-refused-not-done-not-allowed = No se hizo: esta sesión no tiene permiso para hacerlo, sea cual sea la contraseña. Cierra la sesión, vuelve a entrar e inténtalo de nuevo.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Red words when a step was refused because nothing was there to ask for the password; the last sentence says what may help.
common-refused-not-done-unasked = No se hizo: no había nada que pidiera la contraseña de administrador. Cierra la sesión, vuelve a entrar e inténtalo de nuevo.

# SAFETY: needs a human review before it ships
# Red words when a step was refused and it is not known why; the last sentence says what may help.
common-refused-not-done-unclear = No se hizo: no se aceptó la contraseña de administrador, o esta sesión no tiene permiso para hacerlo. Si nada la pidió, cierra la sesión, vuelve a entrar e inténtalo de nuevo.

# Red words when a step behind the administrator's password failed and said nothing of why.
common-refused-no-reason = No se hizo: el paso falló y no dijo por qué.

# Red words when the keyring will not open without the person's password.
common-keyring-locked = El llavero está bloqueado. Cierra la sesión y vuelve a entrar, o desbloquéalo, e inténtalo de nuevo.

# Red words when this computer has no keyring to keep a login or key in.
common-keyring-missing = No hay ningún llavero en este equipo donde guardarlo.

# Red words when the keyring is there and gives no answer in time.
common-keyring-silent = El llavero no respondió a tiempo.

# Red words when work with the keyring never ended, long after its deadline.
common-keyring-never = El llavero nunca respondió.

# Red words when the turn with the keyring could not be taken. { $why } is the system's reason.
common-keyring-turn-failed = No se pudo hacer la consulta al llavero ({ $why }), así que no se le pidió nada.

# Line shown while the keyring has not answered whether it kept or removed a login or key. { $what } is what is kept, such as "login"; { $action } is "removing" or "keeping".
common-keyring-waiting =
    { $action ->
        [removing] El llavero aún no ha respondido, así que de momento no se elimina: { $what }. Si el llavero lo elimina al final, esta línea lo dirá.
       *[other] El llavero aún no ha respondido, así que de momento no se guarda: { $what }. Si el llavero lo guarda al final, esta línea lo dirá.
    }

# Line shown when the keyring answered late and did what was asked. { $what } is what is kept, such as "login"; { $action } is "removing" or "keeping".
common-keyring-late-done =
    { $action ->
        [removing] El llavero respondió tarde: se eliminó { $what }.
       *[other] El llavero respondió tarde: se guardó { $what }.
    }

# Red words when the keyring never answered. { $what } is what is kept, such as "login"; { $action } is "removing" or "keeping".
common-keyring-late-never =
    { $action ->
        [removing] El llavero nunca respondió, así que no se eliminó: { $what }.
       *[other] El llavero nunca respondió, así que no se guardó: { $what }.
    }

# Red words when the keyring answered late and would not do it. { $what } is what is kept, such as "login"; { $action } is "removing" or "keeping"; { $why } is the reason, as a sentence.
common-keyring-late-refused =
    { $action ->
        [removing] El llavero respondió tarde y no eliminó { $what }: { $why }
       *[other] El llavero respondió tarde y no guardó { $what }: { $why }
    }

